# Supplier Service — end-to-end request script (SUP-01 + SUP-02)
#
# Proves list, filter, sort, search, get-by-ID, create, update and deactivate
# for BOTH a student and an admin token, against the Compose stack, no UI (D2 §3).
#
# Run order matters: the first block signs in and captures tokens; later blocks
# reuse them. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" and the IntelliJ HTTP Client
# (both read `# @name` and `{{name.response.body.field}}`).
#
# Prerequisites — bring the stack up first, from the repo root:
#     docker compose up --build
#   user-service → :3001, supplier-service → :3002 (see .env.example host ports).
#
# Written for a FRESH stack. The seeded admin (ADMIN_SEED_EMAILS) starts with the
# bootstrap password and must change it before its first login; the student is
# registered + activated here via the dev mailbox. Re-running against the same DB
# will 409 on register / 403 on the already-changed admin password — reset the DB
# or change @studentEmail to run again.

@userBase = http://localhost:3001
@supplierBase = http://localhost:3002

@adminEmail = admin@u.nus.edu
@bootstrapPassword = dev-only-admin-password-change-me
@adminPassword = Admin-Passw0rd-Changed-01
@studentEmail = sup02.student@u.nus.edu
@studentPassword = Student-Passw0rd-01

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1 · Tokens
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1a · Admin clears the bootstrap password (required before first login)
POST {{userBase}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "currentPassword": "{{bootstrapPassword}}", "newPassword": "{{adminPassword}}" }

### 1b · Admin login → access token
# @name adminLogin
POST {{userBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1c · Register the student
POST {{userBase}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{studentEmail}}", "password": "{{studentPassword}}", "displayName": "SUP-02 Student" }

### 1d · Read the activation token from the dev mailbox (mounted only outside production)
# @name studentMailbox
GET {{userBase}}/dev/mailbox?to={{studentEmail}}

###
@activationToken = {{studentMailbox.response.body.token}}

### 1e · Activate the student account
POST {{userBase}}/auth/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{activationToken}}" }

### 1f · Student login → access token
# @name studentLogin
POST {{userBase}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{studentEmail}}", "password": "{{studentPassword}}" }

###
@studentToken = {{studentLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2 · Create (admin) — a small demo catalogue to list/filter/sort/search over
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2a · Admin creates a FOOD supplier in COM1 (Idempotency-Key makes a retry safe)
# @name createFood
POST {{supplierBase}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sup02-demo-food

{
  "name": "Demo Kopitiam",
  "type": "FOOD",
  "building": "COM1",
  "floor": "1",
  "locationDescription": "Near the north entrance",
  "openingHours": [{ "day": "MON", "opens": "08:00", "closes": "20:00" }],
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/kopitiam.jpg",
  "tags": ["halal", "cheap"]
}

###
@foodId = {{createFood.response.body.supplierId}}
@foodVersion = {{createFood.response.body.version}}

### 2b · Admin creates a CAFE supplier in COM2
POST {{supplierBase}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sup02-demo-cafe

{
  "name": "Demo Cafe",
  "type": "CAFE",
  "building": "COM2",
  "floor": "2",
  "locationDescription": "Beside the seminar rooms",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/cafe.jpg"
}

### 2c · Admin creates a PRINTING supplier in COM1
# @name createPrint
POST {{supplierBase}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sup02-demo-print

{
  "name": "Demo Print Shop",
  "type": "PRINTING",
  "building": "COM1",
  "floor": "1",
  "locationDescription": "Photocopier corner"
}

###
@printId = {{createPrint.response.body.supplierId}}
@printVersion = {{createPrint.response.body.version}}

### 2d · A student may NOT create — expect 403 FORBIDDEN, nothing written
POST {{supplierBase}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Should Fail", "type": "FOOD", "building": "COM1", "floor": "1", "locationDescription": "x" }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3 · List, filter, sort, search (SUP-02) — as a student, then admin
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3a · Student lists the default page (page 1, size 20, name asc)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3b · Admin lists with explicit pagination
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?page=1&pageSize=2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3c · Page size is clamped to 1–100, not rejected (999 → 100)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?pageSize=999
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3d · Filter by type (FOOD)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?type=FOOD
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3e · Filter by building — case-insensitive, canonicalized like create (com1 → COM1)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?building=com1
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3f · Combined filter: PRINTING in COM1
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?type=PRINTING&building=COM1
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3g · Sort by name descending
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?sort=name&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3h · Sort by last-updated, newest first
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?sort=updatedAt&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3i · Case-insensitive search across name/building/location/tags — hits a tag
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?q=HALAL
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3j · Search across the free-text fields
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?q=demo
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 3k · No match → 200 with an empty page (total 0), never 404
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?q=nothing-matches-this
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4 · Get by ID (student and admin)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4a · Student fetches one supplier (detail view adds floor, location, opening hours)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{foodId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 4b · Admin fetches the same supplier
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{foodId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5 · Update (admin) — optimistic lock via If-Match
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5a · Admin updates the FOOD supplier (If-Match carries the version last seen)
# @name updateFood
PUT {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{foodId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{foodVersion}}

{ "floor": "B1", "tags": ["halal", "cheap", "student-favourite"] }

###
@foodVersion2 = {{updateFood.response.body.version}}

### 5b · A student may NOT update — expect 403 FORBIDDEN
PUT {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{foodId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{foodVersion2}}

{ "floor": "3" }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6 · Deactivate (admin) — soft delete; row leaves the listing, stays fetchable
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6a · Admin deactivates the PRINTING supplier
DELETE {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{printId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
If-Match: {{printVersion}}

### 6b · It is gone from the listing …
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers?building=COM1
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 6c · … but still fetchable by ID (active: false)
GET {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{printId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### 6d · A student may NOT deactivate — expect 403 FORBIDDEN
DELETE {{supplierBase}}/suppliers/{{foodId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
If-Match: {{foodVersion2}}
